From 6709bfa0ebc795f8dcd0bf11dbc20e2fa3aac86f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferran Duarri <ferran.duarri@me.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:58:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] sched_ext: bring the v7.3 sched_ext (sub-schedulers,
 cid, arena) to v7.2

kernel/sched/ext/*, include/linux/sched/ext.h, include/trace/events/sched_ext.h and the
scx hunks of sched.h / idle.c / build_policy.c, all from v7.3.1. Needs the cgroup
task-migrate notifier (previous patch). Not taken: cpufreq_schedutil.c and the cpufreq
adjust_perf() max_perf argument, which only schedutil uses and sched_ext doesn't.

One adaptation: v7.3's RCU passes the stalled-CPU mask to scx_rcu_cpu_stall(); 7.2's RCU has
no such mask, so kernel/rcu/tree_stall.h calls it with cpu_none_mask. Effect: a stall report
that aborts a BPF scheduler names no CPU in its exit message; the abort itself still happens.

Forward-Port-Notes: include/linux/sched/ext.h kernel/sched/build_policy.c kernel/sched/ext/arena.c kernel/sched/ext/cid.c kernel/sched/ext/cid.h kernel/sched/ext/ext.c kernel/sched/ext/idle.c kernel/sched/ext/inlines.h kernel/sched/ext/internal.h kernel/sched/ext/sub.c kernel/sched/ext/sub.h kernel/sched/ext/types.h kernel/sched/idle.c kernel/sched/sched.h include/trace/events/sched_ext.h  kernel/rcu/tree_stall.h
Experimental: ADR-009, series.sched73 only.

Signed-off-by: Ferran Duarri <ferran.duarri@me.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
